# {{electronics}} [[programmable read-only memory]]: A PROM chip can be programmed [[write once|one]] or more times (depending on the type) and generally cannot be re-programmed without special equipment.  Once programmed and installed in a device, it functions as a read-only chip (as if it had been [[hard-wired]] to function that way.)

